      },
      "message": "fix(app): generator defect fixes make cached toolpaths stale\n\nA project saved before PR #3684 kept the old cached toolpath of a tabbed\noutside 2D Contour and posted it while reading as current: the stamp's\nwritten rule asked for a new salt only when a verify law changes (#3704).\n\nThe rule decided (option 1, the lean one): a change of generator output\nthat fixes a defect makes old caches stale. It lives at the salt as the\nnamed constant GENERATOR_OUTPUT_VERSION, written into every operation\nstamp. The PR that changes what a generator emits bumps it in the same\nPR; a byte-identical refactor does not. The rule text is in the stamp\ncomment and in docs/decisions/3704-generator-output-version.md.\n\nThe term moves every stamp once (the churn the salt bumps produce): the\ncommitted catalog caches are regenerated (no .nc golden moved), and the\nre-pinned stamp constants of deburr_cache_stamp and wire_stamp are\nre-captured, the same re-pin the v3/v4 salt bumps did.\n\nPins (crates/app/src/operation/stamp_tests.rs):\n- a_bump_of_the_generator_output_version_moves_the_stamp\n- an_unchanged_generator_output_version_keeps_a_saved_cache_current\n- a_tabbed_contour_saved_before_the_bump_reads_stale (the catalog\n  contour-tabs case: a stamp rewritten to the pre-bump value reads\n  Stale on load, the general stale reason, and never posts)\n\nGate: camcraft-app --lib (321 passed), the touched integration suites\n(example_catalog*, plunge_depth_tab, tool_after_state, stale_rapid_law,\ntilt_basis_compat, wire_stamp, deburr_cache_stamp, contour_start_point,\nconformance, first_part_programs, mcp_verify), cargo xtask catalog\n--check, clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings: all green.\n\nFixes #3704",
